16 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Protein sequences and structural diagram of components of the TCR complex. The sequences show specific signaling motifs highlighted in different colors, including ITAMs, BRS, PRS and RK. A schematic on the right illustrates the arrangement of the protein subunits, labeled a, b, e, d, g, and z, showing the membrane-spanning areas and the signaling motifs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating T cell development stages: DN1 to DN4, then DP, leading to mature CD4+ and CD8+ cells. It highlights developmental blockages associated to mutations in eBRS, PRS, RK, and ITAMs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the three stages of T cell receptor \(TCR\) from resting to activation. Stage 1: Unengaged, resting TCR with cholesterol \(Chol\) bound to the TCR and CD45 in close proximity. Stage 2: Ligand-engaged, primed TCR recruits NCK, LCK \(both from the free LCK pool and from the co-receptor-bound pool\). Stage 3: Phosphorylated and active TCR recruits ZAP70 to propagate signaling.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating three pools of LCK in T cells: Free, CD4-LCK, and CD8-LCK. The free LCK pool initiates TCR signaling and is more active and mobile. The LCK in the CD4-LCK pool stabilizes CD4 surface localization and enhances low-affinity antigen response. The LCL in the CD8-LCK increases occupancy during T cell maturation, enhances antigen sensitivity, and stabilizes the TCR-pMHC interaction.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing three kind of TCR-CD3 complexes: alpha-beta, Vgamma9Vdelta2/Vgamma4Vdelta1/Vgamma8Vdelta3/Vgamma3Vdelta1, and Vgamma5Vdelta1/Vgamma2Vdelta1. Each complex interacts with its ligands: pMHC for the alpha-beta TCR-CD3 complex or undefined ligand\(s\) for the gamma-delta TCR-CD3 complexes. The gamma-delta TCR-CD3 complexes are more flexible. The Vgamma9Vdelta2/Vgamma4Vdelta1/Vgamma8Vdelta3/Vgamma3Vdelta1 complexes are monomeric and the Vgamma5Vdelta1/Vgamma2Vdelta1 dimeric.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating three strategies to harness proximal TCR-CD3 signaling mechanisms for generating synthetic receptors. The ligand is recognized using antibody-derived scFv. Strategy 1 harness CD3 tails and their motifs linked to the scFv to generate chimeric antigen receptors \(CARs\). Strategy 2 harness the proximal kinase ZAP70 linked to the scFv. Strategy 3 uses the complete TCR machinery in different formats named eTRUC, AbTCR, and STAR/HIT complexes. Cartoons show the arrangement of the various chains and motifs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
